---
layout: layout.njk
title: Budget Builder
seo_title: "Free Film & TV Production Budget Builder | Tubes"
description: "Build a film or TV production budget online: start with a template, import an existing budget or start from scratch. Totals update automatically. Download as Excel, CSV or PDF. No account needed."
permalink: /tools/budget-builder/
# Geen demo-popup en geen statistiek-script (zie "Gratis tools" in CLAUDE.md).
# Deze tool praat met de eigen server voor de feedbackknop (en, als de
# account-variant aanstaat, voor accounts en versies); server.js geeft
# /tools/budget-builder/ daarom een CSP met connect-src 'self'.
browser_only: true
sections:
  - type: hero
    kicker: Free tool
    title: Build your film or TV *production budget* online
    text: |
      Start with a template, import an existing budget or build one from scratch. Add your expected costs and Tubes keeps the totals up to date automatically.

      When you are ready, download your budget as Excel, CSV or PDF.

      No account needed. Your budget is stored only in this browser and nothing is uploaded to Tubes.
---
{#- Gratis tool "Budget Builder". Bewust géén CMS-secties: het bewerkdeel is te
    specifiek. Tekst wijzig je hier, opmaak staat in style.css (blok "Gratis
    tools: Budget builder", klassen bb-*), logica in js/budget-builder.js. De
    lezer voor xlsx/CSV (import) is js/budget-compare.js, dat als bibliotheek
    meelaadt (window.BudgetCompare). Sjablonen staan in js/budget-templates.js.

    Teksten zijn geschreven vanuit de gebruiker (producent), niet vanuit de
    software: geen JSON, formules of datastructuren in de hoofdteksten; dat
    soort details staat achter "details"-uitklappers of in de FAQ. Movie Magic
    wordt alleen genoemd als naam van het sjabloon, in de importdetails en in
    de FAQ, niet in intro- of begeleidende teksten (wens Joachim).

    data-storage: "local" = versies in de browser (actief); "account" = versies
    op de server met e-mail en wachtwoord (code blijft aanwezig; bij
    terugschakelen ook alle teksten over opslaan aanpassen). -#}

<section class="section theme-white bb-section" id="tool" data-budget-builder data-storage="local" data-max-lines="2000" data-max-versions="10">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="bb-top">
      <div class="bb-top-text">
        <h2>Create your budget</h2>
        <p>Start with a template, import an existing budget or simply add your production costs below.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bb-actions">
        <div class="bb-actions-main">
          <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-open="templates">Start with a template</button>
          <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-open="import">Import budget</button>
          <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-open="export">Download</button>
          <button type="button" class="button button-primary" data-bb-save>Save</button>
        </div>
        <div class="bb-actions-side">
          <span class="bb-account" data-bb-account></span>
          <button type="button" class="bc-link-button" data-bb-open="feedback">Feedback</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {#- Stap 1: sjabloon kiezen. Tegels zolang het budget leeg is; daarna een
        smalle balk met het gekozen sjabloon en een knop om te wisselen. -#}
    <div class="bb-formats" data-bb-formats></div>

    <div class="bb-step-head"><span class="bb-step">2</span><h3>About this budget</h3><span class="bb-help">Give your budget a name and choose the currency, tax rate and date. You can change these later.</span></div>
    <div class="bb-meta">
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-wide">Budget name <input type="text" data-bb-meta="name" placeholder="Draft 1" autocomplete="off"></label>
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-wide">Production <input type="text" data-bb-meta="production" placeholder="Working title" autocomplete="off"></label>
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-small">Currency <select data-bb-meta="currency">
        <option value="EUR">EUR</option>
        <option value="GBP">GBP</option>
        <option value="USD">USD</option>
        <option value="CHF">CHF</option>
        <option value="SEK">SEK</option>
        <option value="NOK">NOK</option>
        <option value="DKK">DKK</option>
        <option value="ISK">ISK</option>
        <option value="PLN">PLN</option>
        <option value="CZK">CZK</option>
        <option value="HUF">HUF</option>
        <option value="RON">RON</option>
        <option value="BGN">BGN</option>
        <option value="CAD">CAD</option>
        <option value="AUD">AUD</option>
      </select></label>
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-small">VAT % <input type="number" data-bb-meta="vat" min="0" max="100" step="0.5" inputmode="decimal"></label>
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-date">Date <input type="date" data-bb-meta="date"></label>
    </div>

    <p class="bb-notice" data-bb-notice role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>

    <div class="bb-layout">
      <div class="bb-main">
        <div class="bb-step-head"><span class="bb-step">3</span><h3>Add your production costs</h3><span class="bb-help">Organise your budget into areas such as crew, equipment, locations, travel and post production. Add as much or as little detail as you need. Tubes calculates the totals automatically.</span></div>
        <div class="bb-sections" data-bb-sections></div>
      </div>

      <aside class="bb-summary" data-bb-summary>
        <div class="bb-step-head"><span class="bb-step">4</span><h3>Review your budget</h3><span class="bb-help">See your current production total and add percentages such as contingency when needed.</span></div>
        <div class="bb-summary-card">
          <span class="bb-label">Total excl. VAT</span>
          <div class="bb-total" data-bb-total>0</div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row"><span>Costs subtotal</span><span class="bb-num" data-bb-subtotal>0</span></div>
          <div class="bb-additionals" data-bb-additionals></div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row bb-sum-add"><button type="button" class="bc-link-button" data-bb-add-additional>+ Add contingency or another percentage</button></div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row bb-sum-total"><span>Total excl. VAT</span><span class="bb-num" data-bb-total-excl>0</span></div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row"><span>VAT <span data-bb-vat-label>21%</span></span><span class="bb-num" data-bb-vat>0</span></div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row bb-sum-last"><span>Total incl. VAT</span><span class="bb-num" data-bb-total-incl>0</span></div>
          <div class="bb-summary-actions">
            <button type="button" class="button button-primary" data-bb-save>Save</button>
            <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-open="export">Download</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bb-share" data-bb-share hidden>
          <span class="bb-label">Share per area</span>
          <div class="bb-share-list" data-bb-share-list></div>
        </div>
        <div class="bb-privacy" data-bb-how>
          <strong>Saving your work</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Your budget is stored in this browser as you work. Close the page and come back later: it is still here.</li>
            <li><strong>Save</strong> keeps a named version on this device, up to ten. Open, rename or delete them under "Saved versions".</li>
            <li>To keep a copy or continue on another computer, download a Tubes budget file and open it there.</li>
            <li>Nothing is uploaded to Tubes. Only the Feedback button sends what you type there.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#- Dialogen: account (alleen in de account-variant), versies, import, sjablonen, download, feedback -#}
  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="account">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3 data-bb-account-title>Save your budget</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">An account keeps up to ten versions of your budget and lets you open them on any device.</p>
    <div class="bb-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button type="button" class="bb-tab is-active" role="tab" data-bb-mode="register" aria-selected="true">Create an account</button>
      <button type="button" class="bb-tab" role="tab" data-bb-mode="login" aria-selected="false">I already have one</button>
    </div>
    <form class="bb-form" data-bb-account-form novalidate>
      <label>Work email <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required inputmode="email"></label>
      <label>Password <input type="password" name="password" autocomplete="current-password" required minlength="8"><span class="bb-help" data-bb-password-help>At least 8 characters</span></label>
      <label class="bb-consent" data-bb-consent-row><input type="checkbox" name="consent"> <span>Store my budget on the Tubes server (EU) and use my email address to reach me about this tool. No newsletter, no sharing with others. <a href="/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy notice</a></span></label>
      <p class="bb-form-error" data-bb-account-error role="alert"></p>
      <button type="submit" class="button button-primary" data-bb-account-submit>Create account and save</button>
    </form>
    <p class="bb-dialog-note">Until you save, the budget only lives in this browser. Saving sends it to your account; you can delete it there at any time.</p>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="versions">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Saved versions</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro" data-bb-versions-intro>Up to ten versions, saved in this browser.</p>
    <div class="bb-versions" data-bb-versions></div>
    <div class="bb-dialog-actions">
      <button type="button" class="button button-primary" data-bb-save-new>Save as new version</button>
      <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-file-save>Download budget file</button>
      <label class="button button-secondary bc-file">Open budget file <input class="visually-hidden" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" data-bb-file-open></label>
      <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-logout>Log out</button>
    </div>
    <p class="bb-dialog-note" data-bb-versions-note>Versions stay on this device. To keep a copy or continue on another computer, download the Tubes budget file and open it there.</p>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="import">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Import an existing budget</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">Import an Excel or CSV file with your costs, or an export from your budgeting software. You can replace your current budget or add the imported costs to it.</p>
    <label class="button button-secondary bc-file">Choose a file <input class="visually-hidden" type="file" accept=".csv,.tsv,.txt,.xlsx" data-bb-import-file></label>
    <p class="bb-form-error" data-bb-import-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="bb-import-preview" data-bb-import-preview hidden>
      <p class="bb-help" data-bb-import-summary></p>
      <div class="bb-dialog-actions">
        <button type="button" class="button button-primary" data-bb-import-apply="replace">Replace current budget</button>
        <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-import-apply="append">Add to current budget</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="bb-dialog-note">Have a Tubes budget file from an earlier download? <label class="bc-link-button bb-inline-file">Open it here<input class="visually-hidden" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" data-bb-file-open></label>.</p>
    <details class="bb-details">
      <summary>Import details</summary>
      <p>Excel and CSV files need a description and an amount per cost; a code column and headings or a section column are used when present. Movie Magic Budgeting exports (.xlsx) are recognised, including the topsheet structure. Each imported cost keeps its amount, shown as quantity 1 at that rate, so your totals stay the same; adjust quantities and rates afterwards if you like.</p>
    </details>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog bb-dialog-wide" data-bb-dialog="templates">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Start with a template</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">Choose a ready made budget structure and adjust it to your production. If the format you normally use is missing, <button type="button" class="bc-link-button" data-bb-open="feedback">let us know</button>.</p>
    <div class="bb-templates" data-bb-templates></div>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="export">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Download your budget</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">Choose the format that works best for you.</p>
    <div class="bb-export-list">
      <button type="button" class="bb-export-item" data-bb-export="xlsx"><strong>Excel</strong><span>An editable spreadsheet with your complete budget and totals.</span></button>
      <button type="button" class="bb-export-item" data-bb-export="csv"><strong>CSV</strong><span>A simple file you can open in spreadsheet software or other tools.</span></button>
      <button type="button" class="bb-export-item" data-bb-export="print"><strong>PDF</strong><span>A clean version of your budget for printing or sharing. Choose "Save as PDF" in the print window.</span></button>
    </div>
    <details class="bb-details">
      <summary>Excel details</summary>
      <p>The Excel file uses the same layout as a budget exported from Tubes: a summary at the top, one row per cost with working formulas, a row per area, and a second sheet with the totals per area. It opens in Tubes as is.</p>
    </details>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="feedback">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Feedback on the Budget Builder</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">Something missing, wrong or confusing? Tell us. It goes straight to the people who build this tool.</p>
    <form class="bb-form" data-bb-feedback-form novalidate>
      <label>Your feedback <textarea name="message" rows="5" required placeholder="What would make this tool more useful for you?"></textarea></label>
      <label>Email <span class="bb-help">(optional, if you would like a reply)</span> <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" inputmode="email"></label>
      <p class="bb-form-error" data-bb-feedback-error role="alert"></p>
      <button type="submit" class="button button-primary" data-bb-feedback-submit>Send feedback</button>
    </form>
    <p class="bb-dialog-note">Your message and email address are stored with our contact messages and used only to follow up on your feedback.</p>
  </dialog>
</section>

{%- set featureText %}
Your budget is only the starting point. In Tubes, you can use the same approved budget to follow purchase orders, invoices and actual costs throughout the production.

This gives you a clear view of what has been spent, what is still expected and how the production is tracking against budget.
{% endset -%}
{%- set section = {
  theme: "teal",
  heading: "Take your budget into production",
  text: featureText,
  image: "/assets/images/tubes-budgeting.png",
  image_alt: "Budgeting in Tubes",
  button: { label: "See how Tubes works", url: "/platform/" }
} -%}
{% include "partials/sections/feature.njk" %}

{%- set section = {
  theme: "white",
  heading: "Questions about the Budget Builder",
  items: [
    { question: "Do I need an account?",
      answer: "No. You can build, save, import and download budgets without an account. Everything happens in your browser." },
    { question: "Can I import an existing budget?",
      answer: "Yes. Import an Excel or CSV file with your costs, or an export from your budgeting software. You can replace your current budget or add the imported costs to it." },
    { question: "Can I import a Movie Magic budget?",
      answer: "Yes. Export your budget from Movie Magic Budgeting as an Excel file and import it here; the categories and accounts come through, including the topsheet structure. You can also start from the Movie Magic template without importing anything." },
    { question: "What can I download?",
      answer: "Excel (an editable spreadsheet in the layout Tubes uses, which also opens in Tubes), CSV, or a PDF via the print window. For a full backup of your work, download a Tubes budget file under Saved versions." },
    { question: "Where is my budget saved?",
      answer: "In your own browser, on this device. The budget you are working on is stored as you type, and Save keeps up to ten named versions next to it. Nothing is uploaded to Tubes. Clearing your browser data removes these budgets, so download a budget file if you want to keep one." },
    { question: "Can I continue working on another computer?",
      answer: "Yes, by taking a file with you. Under Saved versions, choose Download budget file, then open that file on the other computer with Open budget file. Budgets do not move between computers by themselves." },
    { question: "Is the Budget Builder free?",
      answer: "Yes, completely, with no account and no trial period. It is one of the free tools Tubes offers to production teams." },
    { question: "Can I also track actual production costs?",
      answer: "Not in this free tool: the Budget Builder is for preparing a budget. The full Tubes platform adds production finance: cost control, purchase orders, invoices, actuals and forecasting on the same budget. Request a demo to see how that works." }
  ]
} -%}
{% include "partials/sections/faq.njk" %}

{%- set section = {
  title: "Ready to take the budget past the first step?",
  text: "Tubes follows purchase orders, invoices and actual costs against the budget you approved.",
  button: { label: "Request a Demo", url: "/contact/" }
} -%}
{% include "partials/sections/cta.njk" %}

<script src="{{ assets.budgetCompare }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ assets.budgetTemplates }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ assets.budgetBuilder }}" defer></script>
